## Anti Pattern

**1. Exposing API Keys**

Storing API keys in frontend. Exposing in environment variables accessible to client. Keys in version control. Leads to unauthorized usage.

**2. Ignoring Token Limits**

Not tracking token usage. Exceeding context limits. Poor prompt truncation. Wasted tokens.

**3. No Retry Logic**

Single API call attempt. No handling of transient failures. Poor user experience. API errors cause failures.

**4. Overly Long Prompts**

Including unnecessary context. No token budget. High costs. Poor performance. Be concise.

**5. No Response Validation**

Assuming perfect responses. No handling of malformed output. Code breaks. Poor user experience.

## Best Practice

**1. OpenAI Client Setup**

```typescript
// lib/openai.ts
import OpenAI from 'openai';
import { OpenAIError, RateLimitError, APIError } from 'openai/error';

const openai = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY,
  timeout: 60000, // 60 seconds
  maxRetries: 3,
});

// Retry configuration
openai.maxRetries = 3;

// Error handling wrapper
export async function withRetry<T>(
  fn: () => Promise<T>,
  options: {
    maxRetries?: number;
    initialDelay?: number;
    maxDelay?: number;
  } = {}
): Promise<T> {
  const {
    maxRetries = 3,
    initialDelay = 1000,
    maxDelay = 30000
  } = options;

  let lastError: Error | null = null;

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (error) {
      lastError = error as Error;

      if (error instanceof RateLimitError) {
        // Exponential backoff
        const delay = Math.min(initialDelay * Math.pow(2, attempt), maxDelay);
        console.log(`Rate limited. Retrying in ${delay}ms...`);
        await sleep(delay);
      } else if (error instanceof APIError && error.status >= 500) {
        // Retry server errors
        const delay = initialDelay * Math.pow(2, attempt);
        await sleep(delay);
      } else {
        // Don't retry client errors
        throw error;
      }
    }
  }

  throw lastError;
}

// Usage
const response = await withRetry(() =>
  openai.chat.completions.create({
    model: 'gpt-4',
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }]
  })
);
```

**2. Chat Completions**

```typescript
// services/chat.service.ts
interface ChatMessage {
  role: 'system' | 'user' | 'assistant' | 'function';
  content: string | null;
  name?: string;
  function_call?: {
    name: string;
    arguments: string;
  };
}

interface ChatOptions {
  model?: 'gpt-4' | 'gpt-4-turbo' | 'gpt-3.5-turbo';
  temperature?: number;
  maxTokens?: number;
  topP?: number;
  frequencyPenalty?: number;
  presencePenalty?: number;
  stop?: string[];
}

class ChatService {
  async createChat(
    messages: ChatMessage[],
    options: ChatOptions = {}
  ): Promise<OpenAI.Chat.ChatCompletion> {
    const {
      model = 'gpt-4-turbo',
      temperature = 0.7,
      maxTokens = 4096,
      topP,
      frequencyPenalty,
      presencePenalty,
      stop
    } = options;

    return withRetry(() =>
      openai.chat.completions.create({
        model,
        messages,
        temperature,
        max_tokens: maxTokens,
        top_p: topP,
        frequency_penalty: frequencyPenalty,
        presence_penalty: presencePenalty,
        stop,
      })
    );
  }

  // Streaming chat
  async createStreamingChat(
    messages: ChatMessage[],
    options: ChatOptions = {},
    onChunk: (chunk: string) => void
  ): Promise<string> {
    const stream = await openai.chat.completions.create({
      model: options.model || 'gpt-4-turbo',
      messages,
      temperature: options.temperature || 0.7,
      max_tokens: options.maxTokens || 4096,
      stream: true,
    });

    let fullResponse = '';

    for await (const chunk of stream) {
      const content = chunk.choices[0]?.delta?.content;
      if (content) {
        fullResponse += content;
        onChunk(content);
      }
    }

    return fullResponse;
  }

  // Count tokens
  async countTokens(messages: ChatMessage[]): Promise<number> {
    const response = await openai.chat.completions.create({
      model: 'gpt-4',
      messages: messages.map(m => ({ role: m.role, content: m.content || '' })),
      max_tokens: 1,
    });
    
    // Estimate from response
    return response.usage?.total_tokens || 0;
  }
}
```

**3. Function Calling**

```typescript
// Define functions
const functions = [
  {
    name: 'get_weather',
    description: 'Get the current weather in a given location',
    parameters: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        location: {
          type: 'string',
          description: 'The city and state, e.g. San Francisco, CA',
        },
        unit: {
          type: 'string',
          enum: ['celsius', 'fahrenheit'],
        },
      },
      required: ['location'],
    },
  },
  {
    name: 'search_products',
    description: 'Search for products in the catalog',
    parameters: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        query: {
          type: 'string',
          description: 'Search query',
        },
        limit: {
          type: 'integer',
          description: 'Maximum number of results',
          default: 10,
        },
      },
      required: ['query'],
    },
  },
] as const;

class FunctionCallingService {
  async chatWithFunctions(
    userMessage: string,
    context: ChatMessage[] = []
  ): Promise<string> {
    const messages: ChatMessage[] = [
      ...context,
      { role: 'user', content: userMessage }
    ];

    const response = await withRetry(() =>
      openai.chat.completions.create({
        model: 'gpt-4-turbo',
        messages,
        functions,
        function_call: 'auto',
      })
    );

    const message = response.choices[0].message;

    // If model wants to call a function
    if (message.function_call) {
      const functionName = message.function_call.name;
      const args = JSON.parse(message.function_call.arguments);

      // Execute the function
      let functionResult: any;
      switch (functionName) {
        case 'get_weather':
          functionResult = await this.getWeather(args.location, args.unit);
          break;
        case 'search_products':
          functionResult = await this.searchProducts(args.query, args.limit);
          break;
        default:
          throw new Error(`Unknown function: ${functionName}`);
      }

      // Add function result to messages
      messages.push(message);
      messages.push({
        role: 'function',
        name: functionName,
        content: JSON.stringify(functionResult),
      });

      // Get final response
      const finalResponse = await this.createChat(messages);
      return finalResponse.choices[0].message.content || '';
    }

    return message.content || '';
  }

  async getWeather(location: string, unit?: string) {
    // Implementation
    return { location, temperature: '22', unit: unit || 'celsius', condition: 'Sunny' };
  }

  async searchProducts(query: string, limit: number = 10) {
    // Implementation
    return { results: [], query, total: 0 };
  }
}
```

**4. Embeddings**

```typescript
// services/embedding.service.ts
import OpenAI from 'openai';

const openai = new OpenAI();

interface EmbeddingOptions {
  model?: 'text-embedding-3-small' | 'text-embedding-3-large' | 'text-embedding-ada-002';
  dimensions?: number;
  batchSize?: number;
}

interface EmbeddingResult {
  embedding: number[];
  index: number;
}

class EmbeddingService {
  async createEmbedding(
    input: string,
    options: EmbeddingOptions = {}
  ): Promise<number[]> {
    const {
      model = 'text-embedding-3-small',
      dimensions
    } = options;

    const response = await withRetry(() =>
      openai.embeddings.create({
        model,
        input,
        ...(dimensions && { dimensions }),
      })
    );

    return response.data[0].embedding;
  }

  async createBatchEmbeddings(
    inputs: string[],
    options: EmbeddingOptions = {}
  ): Promise<number[][]> {
    const {
      model = 'text-embedding-3-small',
      dimensions,
      batchSize = 100
    } = options;

    const results: number[][] = [];

    // Process in batches (OpenAI limit)
    for (let i = 0; i < inputs.length; i += batchSize) {
      const batch = inputs.slice(i, i + batchSize);
      
      const response = await withRetry(() =>
        openai.embeddings.create({
          model,
          input: batch,
          ...(dimensions && { dimensions }),
        })
      );

      // Sort by index to maintain order
      const sortedEmbeddings = response.data
        .sort((a, b) => a.index - b.index)
        .map(item => item.embedding);
      
      results.push(...sortedEmbeddings);
    }

    return results;
  }

  async createVectorSearchQuery(
    query: string,
    options: EmbeddingOptions = {}
  ): Promise<number[]> {
    return this.createEmbedding(query, options);
  }

  // Calculate cosine similarity
  cosineSimilarity(a: number[], b: number[]): number {
    const dotProduct = a.reduce((sum, val, i) => sum + val * b[i], 0);
    const magnitudeA = Math.sqrt(a.reduce((sum, val) => sum + val * val, 0));
    const magnitudeB = Math.sqrt(b.reduce((sum, val) => sum + val * val, 0));
    
    return dotProduct / (magnitudeA * magnitudeB);
  }
}
```

**5. Cost Management**

```typescript
// services/cost-tracking.service.ts
interface UsageRecord {
  timestamp: Date;
  model: string;
  tokens: {
    prompt: number;
    completion: number;
    total: number;
  };
  cost: number;
}

class CostTrackingService {
  private usage: UsageRecord[] = [];
  private dailyLimit: number;
  private monthlyLimit: number;

  constructor(dailyLimit: number = 100, monthlyLimit: number = 2000) {
    this.dailyLimit = dailyLimit;
    this.monthlyLimit = monthlyLimit;
  }

  // Token pricing (example rates)
  private pricing: Record<string, { prompt: number; completion: number }> = {
    'gpt-4-turbo': { prompt: 10, completion: 30 }, // $10 per 1M input, $30 per 1M output
    'gpt-4': { prompt: 30, completion: 60 },
    'gpt-3.5-turbo': { prompt: 0.5, completion: 1.5 },
    'text-embedding-3-small': { prompt: 0.02, completion: 0 }, // $0.02 per 1M
  };

  recordUsage(usage: OpenAI.CompletionUsage, model: string) {
    const pricing = this.pricing[model] || this.pricing['gpt-4-turbo'];
    
    const promptCost = (usage.prompt_tokens / 1_000_000) * pricing.prompt;
    const completionCost = (usage.completion_tokens / 1_000_000) * pricing.completion;
    
    const record: UsageRecord = {
      timestamp: new Date(),
      model,
      tokens: {
        prompt: usage.prompt_tokens,
        completion: usage.completion_tokens,
        total: usage.total_tokens
      },
      cost: promptCost + completionCost
    };

    this.usage.push(record);

    // Check limits
    this.checkLimits();
  }

  getTodayCost(): number {
    const today = new Date();
    today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
    
    return this.usage
      .filter(u => u.timestamp >= today)
      .reduce((sum, u) => sum + u.cost, 0);
  }

  getMonthCost(): number {
    const monthStart = new Date();
    monthStart.setDate(1);
    monthStart.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
    
    return this.usage
      .filter(u => u.timestamp >= monthStart)
      .reduce((sum, u) => sum + u.cost, 0);
  }

  private checkLimits() {
    if (this.getTodayCost() > this.dailyLimit) {
      console.warn(`Daily cost limit exceeded: $${this.getTodayCost()}`);
    }
    
    if (this.getMonthCost() > this.monthlyLimit) {
      console.error(`Monthly cost limit exceeded: $${this.getMonthCost()}`);
    }
  }

  canMakeRequest(): boolean {
    return this.getTodayCost() < this.dailyLimit && 
           this.getMonthCost() < this.monthlyLimit;
  }
}
```

**6. AI Assistant Implementation**

```typescript
// services/assistant.service.ts
interface AssistantConfig {
  name: string;
  instructions: string;
  model?: string;
  tools?: any[];
  fileIds?: string[];
}

class AssistantService {
  async createAssistant(config: AssistantConfig): Promise<string> {
    const assistant = await openai.beta.assistants.create({
      name: config.name,
      instructions: config.instructions,
      model: config.model || 'gpt-4-turbo',
      tools: config.tools || [{ type: 'code_interpreter' }],
      file_ids: config.fileIds,
    });

    return assistant.id;
  }

  async createThread(): Promise<string> {
    const thread = await openai.beta.threads.create();
    return thread.id;
  }

  async addMessage(
    threadId: string,
    content: string,
    attachments?: { fileId: string; tools: any[] }[]
  ): Promise<string> {
    const message = await openai.beta.threads.messages.create(threadId, {
      role: 'user',
      content,
      attachments,
    });

    return message.id;
  }

  async runAssistant(
    threadId: string,
    assistantId: string,
    additionalInstructions?: string
  ) {
    const run = await openai.beta.threads.runs.create(threadId, {
      assistant_id: assistantId,
      additional_instructions: additionalInstructions,
    });

    return run.id;
  }

  async waitForCompletion(
    threadId: string,
    runId: string
  ): Promise<{ status: string; messages: any[] }> {
    while (true) {
      const run = await openai.beta.threads.runs.retrieve(threadId, runId);

      if (run.status === 'completed') {
        const messages = await openai.beta.threads.messages.list(threadId);
        return { status: 'completed', messages: messages.data };
      }

      if (run.status === 'failed') {
        return { status: 'failed', messages: [] };
      }

      if (run.status === 'requires_action') {
        // Handle function calls
        if (run.required_action?.type === 'submit_tool_outputs') {
          const toolCalls = run.required_action.submit_tool_outputs.tool_calls;
          const toolOutputs = [];

          for (const toolCall of toolCalls) {
            // Execute tool and collect output
            const output = await this.executeToolCall(toolCall);
            toolOutputs.push({
              tool_call_id: toolCall.id,
              output: JSON.stringify(output),
            });
          }

          await openai.beta.threads.runs.submitToolOutputs(
            threadId,
            runId,
            { tool_outputs: toolOutputs }
          );
        }
      }

      await sleep(1000);
    }
  }
}
```

## Workflow

**Phase 1: Requirements Analysis**

Define AI use case. Choose appropriate model. Plan prompt strategy. Estimate costs.

**Phase 2: Implementation**

Set up OpenAI client. Implement API calls. Add error handling. Configure retries.

**Phase 3: Prompt Development**

Design initial prompts. Test with various inputs. Iterate on prompts. Document prompt templates.

**Phase 4: Integration**

Integrate with application. Add caching. Implement streaming. Set up monitoring.

**Phase 5: Testing**

Test with edge cases. Measure latency. Verify responses. User acceptance testing.

**Phase 6: Deployment**

Deploy to production. Set up alerting. Monitor costs. Gather feedback.

